WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.866
Today I'm going to show you how to setup an HTTP or HTTPS load balancer.

00:00:04.533 --> 00:00:06.433
First navigate to networking. 

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.533
Now navigate to load blancing.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.233
Now click start configuration

00:00:10.233 --> 00:00:14.233
in the HTTP/HTTPS Load Balancing section.

00:00:14.966 --> 00:00:16.833
Fill in the name of your load balancer.

00:00:16.833 --> 00:00:19.500
You can use lower case letters, numbers, and hyphens.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:20.666
Click backend

00:00:20.666 --> 00:00:24.266
configuration to configure where your incoming traffic will be redirected

00:00:24.366 --> 00:00:27.400
From the drop down menu you can select an existing backend service or 

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.433
you can create a new backend service.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.000
Now enter the name for your backend service.

00:00:32.133 --> 00:00:33.166
From the backends section

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:34.933
select an instance group. Finally

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.300
select a health check from the drop down at the bottom.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.000
Click and host and path rules from the left panel.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.900
The first row determines where any

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.900
traffic not explicitly with a host and path rule will be sent.

00:00:46.066 --> 00:00:48.266
Click Add host and path rule to add 

00:00:48.266 --> 00:00:50.966
a second row. Now fill it in.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.566
Click frontend configuration to configure the protocol, IP address, 

00:00:54.933 --> 00:00:56.500
port and certificate if necessary

00:00:57.266 --> 00:00:59.833
Click the create button to create your load balancer.

